// onsa.toml
// [test]
// spec = ["§18.1"]

// S-689 (1), S-692 (c): the `impl` whose heading has a name that failed (the type of the `impl`, or a type
// argument of it) is not a heading with an error: the type of `self` is an error type, and each member is a
// unit that is checked (a real error is reported, `self.foo()` and `self + 1` are not). The `impl` whose
// heading has a diagnostic of its own (an E0302 of the type, an E0200 of a bound, a syntax error) is one
// unit, and its members are not checked. The modules take the failed name from a `use` that failed
// (`by_use`), an E0304 (`by_clash`) and a member cut off by a syntax error (`by_cut`); `by_heading_error`
// and `by_syntax` have the headings with a diagnostic.
